# S06-T06: LLM Agent Architecture

## Objective

Design the LLM adapter layer under `server/agents/llm/` reusing `createModelForId` and the
existing `Agent` interface. Document before implementation (T07–T09).

## App-agent preflight (MANDATORY before code)

- [ ] Run MCP preflight per `APP-AGENT-PROTOCOL.md` §2 — **warn user if :3000 down**
- [ ] `explain("integrations")` + `explain("work-control")`
- [ ] Read `intel/DEEP-AI-INTEGRATIONS.md` + `apps/chat/server/api/chats/[id].post.ts` pattern
- [ ] Read `apps/work-control/server/agents/types.ts` + mock implementations

## Implementation (app-agent conventions)

- [ ] Add `apps/work-control/docs/llm-agents.md`: context assembly (chat history, epic, static hints),
  prompt boundaries, mock fallback rules, gate semantics unchanged
- [ ] Define module layout: `server/agents/llm/{root,planner,task}.llm.ts`, shared `context.ts`, `factory.ts`
- [ ] Specify env gate: reuse `validateIntegrations()` — incomplete → mock, no 503 on work-control boot
- [ ] PLANNER output schema: validated `TaskPlan[]` matching role taxonomy from `useAgentRoles()`
- [ ] No code in `core/` except if knowledge update deferred to T05/T11

## Done when (app-agent)

- [ ] `llm-agents.md` reviewed; T07–T09 can implement without ambiguity
- [ ] Architecture respects S06 invariant §7–10

## Out

`apps/work-control/docs/llm-agents.md` (design doc; minimal scaffolding OK if typed stubs only)
